    {
      "text": "I the Lord thy God am a jealous God, Ex. 20:5 (Deut. 5:9; 6:15; Mosiah 11:22). Lord, whose name is Jealous, is a jealous God, Ex. 34:14. spirit of jealousy come upon him, and he be jealous of his wife, Num. 5:14. consumed not the children of Israel in my jealousy, Num. 25:11. God is a consuming fire, even a jealous God, Deut. 4:24. provoked him to jealousy with strange gods, Deut. 32:16. I will move them to jealousy, Deut. 32:21 (Rom. 10:19). provoked him to jealousy with their sins, 1 Kgs. 14:22. moved him to jealousy with their graven images, Ps. 78:58. jealousy is the rage of a man, Prov. 6:34. will be jealous for my holy name, Ezek. 39:25. Lord be jealous for his land, Joel 2:18. I am jealous for Jerusalem and for Zion, Zech. 1:14 (8:2).",
